•	g(x): The actual cost to reach the current node, which is represented by the level of the node (i.e., the number of moves taken).
•	h(x): The heuristic estimate of the remaining cost to reach the goal, which in this case is the number of misplaced tiles (calculated in the h method).
The formula for fval is: f(x)=g(x)+h(x)f(x) = g(x) + h(x) where:
•	g(x) is the number of moves taken (i.e., level of the node).
•	h(x) is the heuristic, which is the number of misplaced tiles between the current state and the goal state.
The fval is used to prioritize nodes in the A* algorithm — nodes with a lower fval are explored first.
