Answer: The formula for f(n) is: f(n)=g(n)+h(n)f(n) = g(n) + h(n) Where:
•	g(n) is the actual cost from the start node to the current node (usually represented by the number of moves or steps taken).
•	h(n) is the heuristic estimate of the cost from the current node to the goal node (such as the number of misplaced tiles or Manhattan distance).
The node with the lowest f(n) value is selected for exploration next.
