5. How does the A algorithm handle nodes already visited or explored?*
Answer: In A*, nodes are placed in one of two lists:
•	Open list: Contains nodes that have been generated but not yet explored.
•	Closed list: Contains nodes that have already been explored.
When a node is generated (as a child of another node), the algorithm checks whether it is already in the open or closed list. If the node is found in the open list and has a higher f(n) value than the one already in the list, the node is skipped. Similarly, if the node is found in the closed list with a lower f(n) value, it is re-added to the open list for further exploration.
This helps A* avoid revisiting and re-exploring less optimal paths.
