•	g(n): The actual cost to reach the current node from the start node. It represents the path cost from the start node to the current node.
•	h(n): The heuristic estimate of the cost from the current node to the goal node. It is an estimate of how far the node is from the goal, based on some heuristic function like Manhattan distance, Euclidean distance, or misplaced tiles.
Together, these values form f(n) = g(n) + h(n), which is used to prioritize nodes in A*.
