7. Can you explain how the A algorithm ensures optimality and completeness?*
Answer: A* ensures optimality when the heuristic function h(n) is admissible, meaning it never overestimates the actual cost to reach the goal. This guarantees that A* will always find the least-cost path.
A* ensures completeness because it will explore all possible paths in the search space, as long as the search space is finite. It will eventually find a solution if one exists, as it checks all nodes in order of increasing f(n).
